## Root cause

Owner: **the product**. `Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/StudyEngine.fs:337-356`, `StagedStudy.engineWith`, requires every fitted path to contain at most one unknown-bearing matrix. AT-1 includes separately observed QZ and LR plus QZ-then-LR observations, so `StudyFitParam.runFit` selects `fitNonlinear` at `:1844-1848`; `scaledProblemWith` then returns `SessionGainNeedsLinearEngineErr` at `:426-438`. This matches the measured LP-LP anchor refusal in `.manifest-arc-runner.log:40836`. Git blame places the restrictive guard in accepted 0386 (`06961376`), with bearer extraction adjusted by 0390 (`a7fd5bf3`); the engine and constructor-test files are unchanged. This is an existing implementation inconsistency exposed by a new test, not a claim that an existing test failed on an unchanged baseline.

The intended linear path already separates constituent fits from the combined-matrix diagnostic (`StudyEngine.fs:1102-1157,1177-1187,1290-1380`). The series regression calls `reconstructLinear` directly (`OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyEngineTests.fs:1887-1910`), bypassing selection. Steps 0386/0390 distinguish genuinely coupled products from a separately reconstructed diagnostic; 0427 explicitly requires the latter through window messages. Its sole authorized source edit is `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/KitAcceptanceTests.fs`. The scope restriction explains why attempt 03 stopped, but is not the numerical cause. The judge and resolver correctly preserve acceptance (`.artifacts/code_judge/0427-01-code-judge.md`, cycle 2; `.artifacts/resolver/0427-resolver-01.md`). The earlier indentation failure was repaired and is not this escalation's cause. The proposed repair is source-traced, **not runtime-verified** here.

